## Confirmed review evidence and reproduction
The guard checks `Extract<Program, PromiseLike<unknown>>` but not Promise-like constituents of `OperationValueOf<Program>`. In the earlier read-only compiler probe, the following wrapped cases accepted and their expected-error directives were unused (TS2578), while the direct Promise negative was rejected. Reproduce against live code before changing it:
```ts
// Each call must become a compile-negative at the appropriate diagnostic line.
resource({
  id: "wrapped", key: (id: string) => [id],
  lookup: () => Effect.succeed(Promise.resolve(1)),
});
transaction({
  id: "wrapped-transaction",
  commit: () => Effect.succeed(Promise.resolve(1)),
});
transaction({
  id: "wrapped-union",
  commit: () => Effect.succeed(Math.random() > 0.5 ? 1 : Promise.resolve(1)),
});
```
Prefer a typed union fixture over randomness in the permanent compiler proof. Promise syntax here is forbidden-input test data, not production interop. Include a structural PromiseLike fixture so this does not test only native Promise.

## Implementation guidance
Derive success once with OperationValueOf<Program>; reject forbidden constituents in that success channel as well as forbidden direct programs. Preserve never/failure-only Effects and exact A/E/R. Keep guards against any/unknown only where required by compiler evidence. Do not blindly delete IsAny/IsUnknown as cosmetic redundancy: prove behavior for direct/wrapped any, unknown, undefined, void, never and mixed unions first. Do not fix by adding runtime Promise execution, erasing channels, rejecting all Effects, or changing the documented operation contract.

## Minimum tests
Both helper-level and public constructor negatives: direct and wrapped Promise/PromiseLike, mixed valid/Promise success union, undefined/void/unknown success. Positives: ordinary value, Effect success and failure-only Effect with exact E/R; no loss of nullable valid values or key-owned P. Retain B03-B05 existing constructor inference cases. Exact expected-error placement must be consumed, not merely put above a multiline call that errors elsewhere.

## Deletion/simplicity receipt
