## Additional accepted token-reflection finding — 2026-09-05
This same private reflection-owner slice also consolidates the duplicate token text readers in [compiler.ts](/Users/arpit/Developer/flow-state/packages/flow-state-rewrite/src/machine/compiler.ts:28) and [behavior.ts](/Users/arpit/Developer/flow-state/packages/flow-state-rewrite/src/machine/behavior.ts:38). Existing allowed files cover both. Remove StateTokenReflection, which prematurely describes unvalidated property values.

One private reader, consumed by both classifiers, has this target behavior:
```ts
const readTokenText = (
  value: unknown,
  key: "kind" | "id" | "name",
): Result.Result<string | undefined, undefined> => {
  if (!Predicate.isObject(value)) return Result.succeed(undefined);

  return Result.try({
    try: () => {
      const descriptor = Object.getOwnPropertyDescriptor(value, key);
      if (descriptor === undefined || !("value" in descriptor)) return undefined;
      return Predicate.isString(descriptor.value) ? descriptor.value : undefined;
    },
    catch: () => undefined,
  });
};
```
This reader is private reflection classification, not the public Diagnostic admission result. Preserve failure versus successful absence; do not collapse it to string | undefined without equivalent classification proof. The two callers have different policies: compiler's foreign token classifier requires state kind/id/name; behavior recognizes its existing token-like cases. Consolidate reading, NOT those classification policies. Getter/proxy, unknown-state versus invalid-state, foreign owner, and nominal identity regression tests must remain unchanged. Keep no duplicate reader or compatibility wrapper after migration.


